# Circle Agent Stack
# Authentication is handled by the Circle CLI itself. There is no Circle API
# key. The demo handles login (email + OTP) and stops for you to accept the
# Terms of Use if your account has not. The CLI stores credentials under
# ~/.circle (override with CIRCLE_CLI_HOME).
# https://developers.circle.com/agent-stack
#
# The agent installs Circle's skills into ~/.agents/skills on its first run and
# reads them from there afterwards, so they are shared with every other agent on
# the machine. There is no chain to configure: the CLI settles each payment on a
# chain the seller and your wallet have in common.

# LLM provider. Required — set ONE of the two keys below. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is
# checked first; if absent, OPENAI_API_KEY is used.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional model override (defaults: anthropic/claude-opus-5 /
# openai/gpt-5.6-sol). Mastra resolves a model from one "provider/model"
# string, so include the prefix — e.g. "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5".
# LLM_MODEL=
